00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:40,500
One of the things that I have had several questions about

154
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:42,500
over the past few weeks

155
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:46,500
is talking about Meribadge, blue cards,

156
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:49,500
And I guess if you want to be really doctrinaire

157
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:51,500
and official about it,

158
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:53,500
this is the application for a Meribadge

159
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:56,500
And the first step with that.

160
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:58,500
when a boy gets a blue card,

161
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:00,500
he brings it to the unit leader for a signature.

162
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:03,500
and what in the world is the unit leader

163
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:04,500
doing? sign in that?

164
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:06,500
Why does the unit leader need to sign

165
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:08,500
an application for a Meribadge?

166
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:11,500
I think it's just so you can see

167
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:13,500
what's being worked on

168
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:16,500
And it's just sort of the keep you in the loop

169
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:19,500
and then I can look for a counselor

170
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:21,500
if they have any problems.

171
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:25,500
I agree with all that Tom said for sure.

172
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:28,500
I guess what I wanted to say is that

173
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:30,500
in scouting

174
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:34,500
those kinds of times are designed to facilitate

175
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:37,500
non-confrontational interaction

176
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:39,500
between the adult and the scout.

177
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,500
It's part of the adult relationship.

178
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:43,500
So Scoutmaster conferences,

179
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,500
signing blue cards,

180
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:47,500
boards of review, things like that

181
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:50,500
kind of institutionalizes the relationship.

182
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:52,500
It's part of the conversation.

183
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:54,500
So let's say, John, he's a second class,

184
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:57,500
He decides to work on his forestry Meribadge.

185
00:07:57,500 --> 00:07:58,500
He gets a blue card.

186
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:00,500
Scoutmaster says why forestry?

187
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,500
And he says he's curious about that

188
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:04,500
And then he says: well,

189
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:06,500
how are you doing on your second class rank?

190
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:08,500
And the scout says: good,

191
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:11,500
Anyway, I only have two more requirements.

192
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:13,500
I'm working on some first class stuff.

193
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:15,500
Scoutmaster signs a blue card,

194
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:17,500
sends a scout on his way.

195
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:19,500
So conversation happened,

196
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,500
a relationship.

197
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,500
I got another example here.

198
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:25,500
Scoutmaster: hi, Freddie,

199
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:27,500
So I see you're interested in starting another Meribadge.

200
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:29,500
Question: how are you doing on the other 11

201
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:31,500
you signed up for?

202
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:34,500
How did you pick this Meribadge?

203
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:36,500
Have you contacted

204
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:39,500
one of the other 11 Meribadge counselors? yet

205
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:42,500
How are you doing on getting to first class?

206
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,500
And then the question:

207
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:47,500
well, do you want to hold off starting another

208
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:50,500
before you finish a couple of other ones?

209
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:52,500
Maybe we could talk about

210
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,500
finishing something

211
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,500
one thing before we start another one.

212
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:59,500
So there's a piece of conversation.

213
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,500
you know things like that

214
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:03,500
And so you know.

215
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:05,500
when he's done,

216
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:07,500
Freddie says: well, I want to start it.

217
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:09,500
then he signs it.

218
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:11,500
And some people are going: well, why would you sign it?

219
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:13,500
Well, that's not the point.

220
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:15,500
The point is they had the conversation.

221
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:17,500
The point is that they interacted.

222
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:19,500
So, just like with the Scoutmaster conference,

223
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:21,500
it's not there to pass the scout,

224
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:23,500
it's there to facilitate the conversation,

225
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:25,500
to facilitate the interaction.

226
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,500
So I don't know.

227
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:29,500
I think that's really important that we do that.

228
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:31,500
By the way, Freddie's a real scout.

229
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,500
That's not his name

230
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:35,500
